Maybe candidate C is strongest overall: decision quality, calm, technical competence, but communication issues could be mitigated? However egocentric and not willing to further education are concerns.\n\nCandidate B's nasty remarks could be a safety risk. I'd lean towards Candidate C as best overall, but need to argue.\n\nWe need to state vote and give reasoning referencing facts.\n\nLet's produce public message: \"I propose Candidate C as the leading candidate because ...\". Provide evidence: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands complicated technology (technical competence), but note concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Compare to others: B's interpersonal issues more severe, D's hot temper, A's lack of openness. So C still best.\n\nOk."}
